.claude

# Machine-local runtime state, never committed: the shipwright, lead-time,
# clustering and slack-roots runners' state and run records, and fleet
# coordination briefs and reports. Ignored here, not only in a user's global
# excludes, so harness-gate's untracked-file refusal (DND-1689) does not fire
# on a machine or a hermetic git config without that global line (DND-1693).
ai-artifacts/

# Claude Code managed-skills sync cache (vendored plugin skills; not harness source)
ai/skills/synced/

# Third-party skills the HyperFrames plugin's installer (`npx hyperframes
# skills update <name>`) copies into ~/.claude/skills, which resolves to the
# main checkout's ai/skills/ (DND-1960). The installer records its set as the
# `.skills` keys of ~/.agents/.skill-lock.json. One line per skill, never a
# pattern: `ai/skills/*` or `ai/skills/hyperframes*` would also hide a new
# first-party skill, and `git add -A` would skip it with no error. A name the
# installer adds later dirties the main checkout until its line lands here:
# every shipwright tick yields, and check-guard-messages, check-bin-help and
# check-tool-risk fail when run there. After 3 hourly STALE skips (dirt
# unchanged 6h) the shipwright's stale-dirt alert (DND-692) names the path.
# ai/test/vendored-skills-ignore/self-test.sh checks each name below is
# ignored and that a broad pattern does not hide a new first-party skill.
/ai/skills/faceless-explainer/
/ai/skills/hyperframes/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-animation/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-audio/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-cli/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-core/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-creative/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-keyframes/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-registry/
/ai/skills/hyperframes-studio/
/ai/skills/media-use/

# Shipwright working notes: proposals/analyses kept as local durable scratch,
# not committed harness source.
ai/proposals/

# harness-eval transient run output (baseline.json is the committed reference)
ai/eval/scorecard.json

# harness-metrics transient output (prices.json, if added, is committed config)
ai/telemetry/metrics.json
